<h2>1. What cookies are</h2>
<p>
	Cookies are small text files that a website may store on your device when you visit. They are used to
	“remember” settings, recognise a user between visits or collect statistics about how the site is used.
	Similar functions can be performed by other browser storage technologies (localStorage, sessionStorage) or
	by embedded third-party content.
</p>

<h2>2. What this Website uses</h2>
<div class="callout">
	<p>
		<strong>In its current version the Website does not set cookies and does not use tracking
		technologies.</strong> A consent banner is therefore not displayed.
	</p>
</div>
<p>In particular:</p>
<ul>
	<li>no analytics or statistics tools are used (e.g. Google Analytics);</li>
	<li>no marketing or advertising cookies or pixels are used;</li>
	<li>fonts and all resources are served from the Website's own server, not from external services;</li>
	<li>no interactive map or other third-party content is embedded;</li>
	<li>the contact form does not store data in your browser.</li>
</ul>
<p>
	The only information stored in your browser is your language preference (Bulgarian or English), which is
	kept in the browser's local storage, is not transmitted to any server and is not used for tracking.
	The technical server logs of the hosting provider are described in the
	<a href="/politika-za-poveritelnost">Privacy Policy</a>.
</p>

